WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:15.496
Mowgli explained his plan to Akela.

2
00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.758
Then Akela and Gray Brother got to work.

3
00:00:21.658 --> 00:00:25.099
The two wolves ran in and out of the herd of buffalo.

4
00:00:26.299 --> 00:00:28.760
They separated the herd into two groups.

5
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:33.338
The females and young buffalo were in one group.

6
00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:37.381
They glared and pawed, ready to attack the wolves.

7
00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:41.544
The male buffalo stood together in the other group.

8
00:00:42.785 --> 00:00:45.267
They were bigger and looked more threatening.

9
00:00:46.628 --> 00:00:49.991
But Mowgli knew they were less dangerous than the females.

10
00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:53.973
The males had no young calves to protect.

11
00:00:55.034 --> 00:00:57.116
Mowgli slipped onto Rama's back.

12
00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:04.619
"Akela, drive your herd left, toward the head of this big ravine.

13
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.522
Gray Brother, drive the females to the ravine's other end.

14
00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:13.584
Keep them there till we come down."

15
00:01:14.904 --> 00:01:17.566
Akela howled and his group took off.

16
00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:22.529
Gray Brother began to lead the females in the opposite direction.

17
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:28.512
Meanwhile some of the village children were watching the scene.

18
00:01:29.824 --> 00:01:33.887
They hurried home with the cattle as fast as their legs could carry them.

19
00:01:33.907 --> 00:01:36.229
"The buffalo have gone mad.

20
00:01:36.709 --> 00:01:37.870
They're running away!"

21
00:01:39.191 --> 00:01:40.732
Mowgli's plan was simple.

22
00:01:41.653 --> 00:01:45.776
He planned to trap Shere Khan in the ravine, between the two herds.

23
00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:49.158
Shere Khan had just eaten a large meal.

24
00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:54.182
It would be hard for him to fight or climb up the sides of the ravine.

25
00:01:59.804 --> 00:02:03.585
Mowgli rounded up the confused males at the head of the ravine.

26
00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:08.506
They stood on a grassy slope that led down to the ravine.

27
00:02:08.526 --> 00:02:14.568
"Good," Mowgli thought, looking at the sides of the ravine.

28
00:02:15.628 --> 00:02:18.289
The sides ran nearly straight up and down.

29
00:02:18.949 --> 00:02:20.630
Thick vines hung over them.

30
00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.791
That would make it even harder for the tiger to climb out.

31
00:02:26.151 --> 00:02:30.256
Mowgli held up a hand to signal Akela.

32
00:02:30.296 --> 00:02:34.439
Then he put his hands to his mouth and shouted down the ravine.

33
00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.661
"Shere Khan!"

34
00:02:37.261 --> 00:02:39.363
Echoes jumped from rock to rock.

35
00:02:42.205 --> 00:02:43.886
A snarl echoed back.

36
00:02:43.906 --> 00:02:45.907
"Who calls me?"

37
00:02:45.927 --> 00:02:49.770
"It's me—Mowgli!"

38
00:02:50.551 --> 00:02:51.791
He turned to Akela.

39
00:02:51.811 --> 00:02:54.053
"Bring the herd down now!

40
00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:55.954
Down, Rama, down!"

41
00:02:56.515 --> 00:02:57.756
he commanded the buffalo.

42
00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.501
The male herd stood at the edge of the slope.

43
00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.664
Akela gave a hunting yell, and they fell forward.

44
00:03:06.444 --> 00:03:11.327
They fell, one after the other, like boulders crashing down during a flood.

45
00:03:13.228 --> 00:03:16.670
In the ravine Rama quickly caught Shere Khan's scent.

46
00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:22.733
Now the buffalo knew what their job was—it was a charge against a tiger.

47
00:03:24.854 --> 00:03:27.376
Shere Khan first heard a thunder of hooves.

48
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.902
He picked himself up and looked from side to side, trying to find a way out of the

49
00:03:33.942 --> 00:03:39.745
ravine. But its walls were straight and full of twisting vines.

50
00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:45.087
And he was still sleepy and heavy from his large meal.

51
00:03:46.527 --> 00:03:49.289
The stampede splashed through a pool of water.

52
00:03:50.149 --> 00:03:52.070
The animals bellowed loudly.

53
00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:57.252
Mowgli heard a reply from the females at the other end of the ravine.

54
00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.502
Shere Khan turned to look toward the females too.

55
00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:07.225
Then the tiger whirled back toward the males.

56
00:04:08.346 --> 00:04:24.755
The tiger knew by instinct that it was better to face them than any protective Just then Rama

57
00:04:24.835 --> 00:04:25.956
tripped and stumbled.

58
00:04:28.192 --> 00:04:31.793
The beasts behind him crashed hard into the approaching females.

59
00:04:32.713 --> 00:04:38.175
Soon both herds were charging through the ravine, stamping and snorting as they ran.

60
00:04:39.355 --> 00:04:41.156
Mowgli slipped off Rama's neck.

61
00:04:41.176 --> 00:04:42.956
"Quick, Akela!

62
00:04:43.396 --> 00:04:46.077
Break them up before they start fighting one another."

63
00:04:47.238 --> 00:04:51.679
Akela and Gray Brother ran around the buffalo, trying to separate them.

64
00:04:53.039 --> 00:04:55.580
Suddenly the herd turned toward Mowgli.

65
00:04:57.728 --> 00:05:00.292
They were ready to charge through the ravine again.

66
00:05:02.575 --> 00:05:04.217
But Mowgli held up his hand.

67
00:05:04.878 --> 00:05:06.921
Shere Khan was already dead.

68
00:05:08.783 --> 00:05:11.788
Soon hungry birds would be coming for him.
